caption: Procedures — Overview
technology-rule: overview

Tech Level describes what can exist and how mature it is. Facility grade describes what can be installed or repaired locally. Advanced cybernetics can function in a low-TL setting even when proper repair is unavailable.

| TL | Cybernetic Era | Typical Capabilities |
| --- | --- | --- |
| TL8 | Advanced prosthetics | Medical implants, powered prosthetics, early neural links |
| TL9 | True cybernetics | Bionic limbs, cyber-eyes, chip slots, implant radios, subdermal armor |
| TL10 | Mature cybernetics | Combat limbs, pain editors, cyberdecks, power spines, practical chassis bodies |
| TL11 | Transhuman cybernetics | Parallel processors, self-repair, reliable full conversion, advanced nanomedicine |
| TL12 | Miracle cybernetics | Living metal, energy-weave skin, posthuman bodies, metamorphic systems |
| TL^ | Superscience | Antigravity, reactionless thrust, force screens, stasis, disintegrators, cyber-soul systems |

| Procedure | Typical Work | Base Time | Typical Recovery | Minimum Facility |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Simple | Surface port, small monitor, identification implant | About 15 minutes | Hours | 1 |
| Minor | Datajack, injector, simple cyber-ear, small interface | About 1 hour | About 1 day | 2 |
| Major | Limb, cyber-eye, organ, chip slot, subdermal armor | About 2 hours | About 1 week | 3 |
| Radical | Full-body integration, major brain work, Class III conversion | About 4 hours or more | Several weeks | 4 |
| Metamorphic | TL12 reconstruction, divine body work, cyber-soul transfer | Varies | Hours to weeks | 5 |

| Grade | Facility | Can Usually Install | Can Usually Repair |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | No cyberclinic | Nothing; stabilization only | Crude bracing and biological first aid |
| 1 | Emergency cyber-med station | Simple procedures | Diagnostics, recharge, temporary patches |
| 2 | Frontier clinic | Minor procedures and basic restoration | Common hands, ports, organs, and standard cells |
| 3 | Standard cyberclinic | Major procedures and common performance ware | Limbs, chip slots, subdermal armor, neural interfaces |
| 4 | Advanced center | Radical surgery, military suites, Class III bodies | Warbodies, complex neural systems, prototypes |
| 5 | Nanofac / divine forge / miracle laboratory | TL12, total conversion, living-machine and cyber-soul work | Miracle reconstruction and source-specific systems |

| Improvised Help | What It Can Do | What It Usually Cannot Do |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Healer or physician | Treat infection, shock, tissue damage, and rejection | Repair actuators, firmware, or processors |
| Blacksmith or machinist | Brace a limb, replace simple metal parts | Calibrate neural interfaces |
| Material Mage | Repair casing, structure, or living metal | Restore software or medical integration without relevant skill |
| Lightning Mage | Recharge a power cell | Safely regulate voltage or repair damage |
| Alchemist | Provide coolant, anti-rejection drugs, or nanite feedstock substitutes | Rebuild complex electronics |
| Divine forge | Repair compatible sacred or soul-attuned systems | Automatically understand unrelated corporate cyberware |

MINIMUM VS. MATURE TL

Minimum TL permits prototypes or rare systems. Mature TL means compact, reliable, supportable, and reasonably available.
